WEBVTT

00:11.469 --> 00:14.639
I don't know
who I'll be traveling with yet.

00:14.723 --> 00:16.850
They refused to tell me.

00:17.767 --> 00:20.562
I've been wondering who it might be.

00:21.354 --> 00:23.982
The mystery makes this trip
that much more thrilling.

00:25.608 --> 00:29.696
It's like something that only happens
in movies is happening to me.

00:30.447 --> 00:34.242
Anyway, I'm really nervous but excited.

00:43.168 --> 00:45.253
Hold this. It's warm.

00:58.308 --> 01:00.143
I think the reason every moment

01:00.643 --> 01:03.188
of our journey has been beautiful…

01:05.607 --> 01:07.275
is that you

01:07.942 --> 01:09.944
were a part of the scenery.

01:17.744 --> 01:21.956
But there's a scene in this movie I like,
where they go to the opera.

01:23.291 --> 01:26.336
Do you know Pretty Woman,
the movie with Julia Roberts?

01:28.338 --> 01:31.883
Next time, let's go see
that opera you memorized.

01:34.511 --> 01:35.762
Delicious.

01:35.845 --> 01:37.639
-Mix.
-Mix.

01:37.722 --> 01:39.808
-Yay, cheers!
-Cheers!

01:53.488 --> 01:54.781
Beautiful.

01:56.491 --> 01:58.159
So much that I can't look away.

01:59.911 --> 02:00.829
I…

02:03.706 --> 02:06.126
really like you, Cha Mu-hee.

02:30.191 --> 02:31.609
-Wasn't that great?
-Yeah.

02:35.196 --> 02:38.116
That's just the rough cut,
but what do you think? Romantic, huh?

02:40.493 --> 02:43.496
When it comes to on-screen romances,

02:43.580 --> 02:46.666
viewers are used to them,
so they don't expect them to be real.

02:46.749 --> 02:49.919
Unless you really start dating
and it becomes a story, of course.

02:50.503 --> 02:52.213
But you aren't dating, are you?

02:54.799 --> 02:58.428
To be frank, it'd be best
to broadcast the show as is,

02:58.928 --> 03:01.514
but if this will hurt either of you,
we'll edit it.

03:02.098 --> 03:04.475
Sure, we had that bet on the table,

03:04.559 --> 03:07.604
but we're not thugs
who exploit someone's genuine feelings.

03:10.815 --> 03:13.651
It's fine with me. I don't mind.

03:14.986 --> 03:17.363
Did you just… understand what I said?

03:17.447 --> 03:18.531
Yes.

03:18.615 --> 03:21.326
Wow, Hiro!
How did you get so good at Korean?

03:31.836 --> 03:33.046
To tell you the truth,

03:33.922 --> 03:37.592
I liked you from the second time
we ran into each other.

03:38.676 --> 03:40.011
And

03:40.553 --> 03:43.389
when I found out
you were Jin-suk's brother,

03:44.098 --> 03:46.142
I felt a little awkward and embarrassed,

03:47.393 --> 03:49.479
in case you knew I'd liked you.

03:49.562 --> 03:51.648
I was always careful around you.

03:54.108 --> 03:55.276
In case you'd catch on.

03:58.780 --> 03:59.739
Then,

04:00.949 --> 04:03.451
Ho-jin, did you really like me?

04:03.952 --> 04:04.786
I did.

04:07.288 --> 04:10.208
I never thought the day would come
when I'd be telling you this.

04:12.293 --> 04:14.170
Seeing how comfortable I feel telling you,

04:15.046 --> 04:17.674
it seems the zombie movie
I thought would never end

04:18.174 --> 04:21.261
has finally come to an end,
once and for all.

04:23.388 --> 04:24.222
Zombie movie?

04:28.768 --> 04:30.019
Two hours until Busan.

04:30.770 --> 04:34.482
If I'm to clear the air in that time
and avoid any misunderstandings,

04:35.191 --> 04:37.652
I'd best start with what happened
on Enoshima Island.

04:38.236 --> 04:40.613
Right, the photo of you on that island.

04:41.990 --> 04:45.285
Mu-hee took that photo, didn't she?

04:47.036 --> 04:47.870
That's right.

04:49.956 --> 04:51.416
That's where I first met her.

04:52.041 --> 04:53.793
There, on that day.

04:57.422 --> 05:00.717
You said you wanted revenge,
so I thought you'd ask them to cut it all.

05:01.217 --> 05:02.969
Thanks for signing off on it.

05:03.469 --> 05:04.679
No need to thank me.

05:05.179 --> 05:08.099
That's not how I'll take revenge.

05:09.392 --> 05:11.144
Then how will you?

05:14.105 --> 05:15.440
I'm going to stitch you out.

05:16.733 --> 05:17.567
What?

05:18.234 --> 05:19.235
Not that.

05:20.778 --> 05:22.113
I'm going to snitch on you.

05:24.699 --> 05:26.075
About what?

05:27.744 --> 05:29.829
I'm going to spill the beans
about everything.

05:30.788 --> 05:32.749
That you hit on me.

05:33.333 --> 05:34.334
To whom?

05:34.917 --> 05:36.419
You dummy. Who else?

05:36.961 --> 05:41.924
He's great at Japanese,
so it'll be easy for me to snitch on you.

05:42.717 --> 05:43.926
Mr. Joo Ho-jin?

05:44.010 --> 05:45.053
Yeah.

05:45.136 --> 05:46.387
He already…

05:48.514 --> 05:49.390
knows everything.

05:50.224 --> 05:51.059
He does?

05:51.142 --> 05:52.643
I told him myself.

05:53.978 --> 05:55.104
I even asked him

05:55.897 --> 05:57.940
to help me make things work with you.

05:59.609 --> 06:02.195
You actually said all that
to the guy you like?

06:02.278 --> 06:03.529
Are you seriously…

06:04.238 --> 06:05.156
Are you stupid?

06:06.824 --> 06:08.368
I'm not stupid.

06:08.451 --> 06:09.577
I'm crazy.

06:11.788 --> 06:14.916
Just think of me as a madwoman
like Do Ra-mi.

06:15.792 --> 06:18.795
I was planning to tease you,
but you're no fun.

06:22.507 --> 06:23.341
Hiro.

06:23.883 --> 06:25.259
You were dashing.

06:26.094 --> 06:28.888
You were even more dashing on screen.

06:28.971 --> 06:30.056
I know.

06:33.684 --> 06:36.270
That's what I thought
throughout the entire shoot.

06:36.813 --> 06:38.606
How wonderful it would be

06:38.689 --> 06:42.193
if dating were nothing but happiness
and beautiful views

06:42.276 --> 06:43.945
with a great guy like you.

06:45.196 --> 06:47.782
Nothing to worry or feel anxious about.

06:49.575 --> 06:53.413
And, at the end of it all,
we even had a happy ending.

06:56.082 --> 06:58.000
I guess that's why Do Ra-mi…

06:59.752 --> 07:00.753
I mean,

07:01.462 --> 07:03.256
why I did that to you.

07:11.764 --> 07:12.890
It's my fault.

07:13.891 --> 07:15.768
I hit on you.

07:16.269 --> 07:17.520
It was me.

07:20.106 --> 07:21.023
I'm sorry.

07:23.234 --> 07:24.402
And thank you.

07:25.820 --> 07:27.113
You were…

07:29.782 --> 07:33.578
the prince from my dreams
I longed to meet…

07:35.663 --> 07:37.248
as an escape from my reality.

07:44.380 --> 07:45.256
Did you get that?

07:47.925 --> 07:50.261
I don't know. I don't understand.

07:51.512 --> 07:52.889
You totally understood!

07:52.972 --> 07:56.225
You must be a genius.
How'd you get fluent in Korean so quickly?

07:56.309 --> 07:57.852
You're awesome.

08:01.063 --> 08:03.524
When I met you
by the clock tower in Italy,

08:04.400 --> 08:07.153
and when you asked me if I liked you…

08:08.738 --> 08:12.283
I've wondered what might have been
if I'd just been honest and said yes.

08:13.826 --> 08:16.162
I regretted not having done so.

08:19.624 --> 08:22.460
I'm so bitter about that.

08:28.674 --> 08:29.550
I'm sorry.

08:32.011 --> 08:34.555
I don't understand Japanese at all.

08:42.146 --> 08:42.980
You're…

08:45.441 --> 08:46.526
an idiot.

08:48.110 --> 08:49.111
What?

08:56.035 --> 08:58.913
My mom's here to pick me up,
so I'm heading that way.

08:58.996 --> 09:01.749
Okay, I'm going to go catch a cab.

09:03.209 --> 09:04.043
See you.

09:06.337 --> 09:07.296
See you.

09:51.924 --> 09:56.596
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

09:58.180 --> 10:01.225
I heard you were looking for a place
to donate the antique books

10:01.309 --> 10:03.644
that belonged to Mr. Yoon Won-jae.

10:04.186 --> 10:07.982
I was thinking our university library
might be an apt place,

10:08.065 --> 10:10.484
and I was looking into the matter
through Mr. Oh.

10:11.068 --> 10:14.155
I never imagined
you would personally step in, Mr. Kim.

10:14.238 --> 10:15.656
Thank you.

10:15.740 --> 10:17.491
-You see--
-Listen.

10:19.327 --> 10:21.287
I'm not here about that.

10:22.413 --> 10:25.666
I actually came to ask you something
about your youngest brother.

10:29.420 --> 10:32.131
You came to ask about my brother
who died years ago?

10:33.341 --> 10:34.800
He left behind a daughter, no?

10:35.760 --> 10:37.845
Who you adopted.

10:38.929 --> 10:40.014
Is that girl…

10:42.767 --> 10:44.352
Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

10:49.482 --> 10:50.858
Yes, she is.

10:52.610 --> 10:54.820
Well, I just thought it was a little odd.

10:54.904 --> 10:56.656
Mr. Oh here told me

10:57.156 --> 10:59.450
that he died when he was very young.

10:59.533 --> 11:02.119
-From a serious illness.
-Yes, from a serious illness.

11:02.620 --> 11:04.080
But Ms. Cha Mu-hee said

11:04.580 --> 11:07.083
her parents died in an accident.

11:07.708 --> 11:09.126
Mr. Kim.

11:10.044 --> 11:13.005
Do you know Mu-hee well?

11:15.174 --> 11:16.676
Yes, we've crossed paths.

11:16.759 --> 11:20.721
We dined together
and even attended a concert together.

11:20.805 --> 11:22.765
Right, we both saw her.

11:23.265 --> 11:26.394
We were caught between Ms. Cha
and Mr. Yoon's grandson.

11:26.477 --> 11:28.396
-Such a cute couple.
-That's enough.

11:30.523 --> 11:34.110
Mr. Yoon's grandson is like a son to me.

11:35.027 --> 11:36.862
I was just a bit concerned.

11:37.530 --> 11:39.990
Goodness, please don't take offense.

11:40.074 --> 11:41.867
If he's like a son to you,

11:41.951 --> 11:44.161
please dissuade him
from associating with Mu-hee.

11:45.830 --> 11:46.914
Dissuade him?

11:48.040 --> 11:49.291
She may be adopted,

11:49.375 --> 11:52.378
but isn't Ms. Cha Mu-hee your daughter?

11:53.504 --> 11:56.424
We took her in
because she's part of our family,

11:57.007 --> 11:58.092
but even we

11:59.093 --> 12:00.594
didn't want to let that child

12:01.095 --> 12:03.097
anywhere near us.

12:06.267 --> 12:07.184
Yes.

12:07.893 --> 12:09.645
I'm at the station near my place.

12:09.729 --> 12:10.896
But it's so late.

12:11.731 --> 12:12.815
Not at all.

12:13.315 --> 12:15.943
The later the better,
what with fewer people around.

12:16.736 --> 12:18.863
Still, it's past midnight.

12:19.405 --> 12:21.866
Shouldn't you get to sleep early
since you work tomorrow?

12:23.033 --> 12:24.577
Mr. Joo Ho-jin, are you tired?

12:26.162 --> 12:29.415
Well, you did work all day
and started early.

12:29.498 --> 12:31.000
You must be pretty tired.

12:33.461 --> 12:36.338
Still, didn't you get some shut-eye
on the train?

12:37.965 --> 12:41.510
Never mind. Sleeping on the train
doesn't count as real sleep, does it?

12:43.304 --> 12:46.265
If you're tired,
you should go home and rest.

12:56.817 --> 12:57.902
I slept on the train.

12:57.985 --> 13:01.280
I'm not tired at all,
and thank you for coming to see me.

13:01.989 --> 13:04.742
How did you know? Did you see me?

13:05.618 --> 13:08.078
You kept rambling,
so I figured you were here.

13:10.539 --> 13:12.833
Well, you were so late getting back.

13:13.417 --> 13:16.545
I came here and waited
so we wouldn't waste any time.

13:17.755 --> 13:18.589
Well done.

13:21.550 --> 13:22.510
Your hand is cold.

13:22.593 --> 13:24.637
You waited out in the cold,

13:25.888 --> 13:26.972
only to leave?

13:28.224 --> 13:29.099
Well,

13:29.183 --> 13:32.728
I didn't tell you I was coming,
so I was just going to go.

13:33.354 --> 13:34.188
Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

13:39.026 --> 13:41.278
I'm going to spell this out for you,
so listen up.

13:44.323 --> 13:46.075
I like you so much

13:46.575 --> 13:50.079
that I would come see you
even after three sleepless nights.

13:55.459 --> 13:57.086
But not four. I might drop dead.

14:02.007 --> 14:03.551
Anywhere you want to go?

14:03.634 --> 14:05.928
There's actually a place
I want to show you.

14:20.901 --> 14:22.486
I love this place.

14:23.404 --> 14:25.364
The night view isn't bad, is it?

14:26.824 --> 14:29.034
I just wish we could have seen
the stars better.

14:30.411 --> 14:31.662
Do you want to see stars?

14:32.454 --> 14:34.665
I know a great spot for stargazing.

14:35.499 --> 14:36.333
Where?

14:36.417 --> 14:39.879
There's something called
the International Dark Sky Association.

14:40.671 --> 14:42.631
Dark Sky Association? That's a thing?

14:43.215 --> 14:46.135
They're dedicated to protecting
the beauty of the night sky

14:46.218 --> 14:47.887
from light pollution.

14:48.387 --> 14:52.141
The first place they designated
as a dark-sky preserve in Asia

14:52.641 --> 14:53.684
is in Korea.

14:55.728 --> 14:59.356
Sort of like how the Michelin Guide
gives stars to go-to restaurants?

14:59.440 --> 15:00.274
Exactly.

15:00.774 --> 15:02.234
A go-to spot for stars.

15:02.860 --> 15:05.487
They say you can see the Milky Way
clearly from there.

15:05.988 --> 15:07.323
The Milky Way?

15:07.823 --> 15:10.659
I know about it,
but I've never seen it properly.

15:10.743 --> 15:12.786
-Want to go see it together?
-Sure.

15:13.954 --> 15:16.665
We saw the Northern Lights,
so let's see the Milky Way too.

15:18.000 --> 15:21.670
I hope the weather is good.
I should collect more clovers.

15:22.254 --> 15:23.839
Sure, do your best.

15:24.715 --> 15:26.008
If you think about it,

15:27.134 --> 15:30.596
being taller means
you're slightly closer to the sky.

15:31.180 --> 15:33.933
Then I guess
you'd have a better view of the stars.

15:34.433 --> 15:36.560
No way. Want to check?

15:38.479 --> 15:39.730
Here we go!

15:44.276 --> 15:46.654
Be careful. So, can you see them better?

15:47.196 --> 15:49.281
I can see them much better.

16:42.876 --> 16:45.421
-All right. Glasses full, ladies?
-Sure.

16:45.504 --> 16:48.298
Let's celebrate
Shin Ji-sun's broken engagement.

16:48.382 --> 16:51.010
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

16:51.927 --> 16:55.264
Don't be embarrassed, okay?
Better to call it off than end in divorce.

16:55.347 --> 16:56.932
-Yeah.
-What are you saying?

16:57.016 --> 16:59.476
You could call it off ten times over.
It means nothing.

16:59.977 --> 17:01.645
This one here got a divorce.

17:01.729 --> 17:02.604
It's fine.

17:02.688 --> 17:05.190
Hey, want me to introduce you to a guy?

17:05.274 --> 17:09.111
One of my husband's friends
owns a small building in Seoul.

17:09.611 --> 17:12.489
He's really tall and handsome too.

17:12.990 --> 17:14.283
Wanna meet him?

17:14.366 --> 17:16.952
Forget it.
Ji-sun doesn't need us to set her up.

17:17.036 --> 17:20.581
I'm sure she's surrounded
by hot guys all the time.

17:20.664 --> 17:23.083
Ji-sun, date a celebrity next time.

17:23.167 --> 17:26.128
-Yeah!
-A good-looking, older man.

17:27.588 --> 17:29.965
Don't you girls worry.

17:30.049 --> 17:31.300
I already met someone.

17:31.800 --> 17:32.968
-Really?
-Really?

17:33.052 --> 17:33.969
Yeah!

17:34.053 --> 17:38.348
He's tall, really good-looking, and young.

17:38.432 --> 17:39.433
He's younger than me.

17:39.933 --> 17:41.810
Shin Ji-sun, you've still got it!

17:43.020 --> 17:46.190
-Got any pics? Show us.
-Yeah, let's see this young hunk.

17:46.273 --> 17:47.232
You wanna see him?

17:47.316 --> 17:48.442
-Yeah.
-Of course.

17:48.525 --> 17:49.902
I'll show you.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.653
-She's gonna show us.
-Let's see him.

17:57.743 --> 17:58.994
Kim Yong-u?

17:59.078 --> 18:02.414
I was looking for him in here,
so what's he doing over there?

18:05.501 --> 18:06.835
Hello.

18:07.753 --> 18:10.631
I'm the young hunk she's dating.

18:12.299 --> 18:13.842
He is good-looking.

18:13.926 --> 18:15.427
Hello.

18:28.649 --> 18:30.109
-Here.
-How'd this happen?

18:30.192 --> 18:33.070
You said in your text
that you were drinking at the market.

18:33.153 --> 18:34.571
I searched the whole market.

18:34.655 --> 18:37.366
And why exactly did you come all this way?

18:38.784 --> 18:40.786
I came to tell you something important,

18:40.869 --> 18:43.288
and I somehow showed up
at the perfect time.

18:49.044 --> 18:50.295
When I told them

18:51.213 --> 18:53.215
I broke off my engagement,

18:54.174 --> 18:58.387
my friends were trying to comfort me,
so I was just showing off a bit.

18:58.470 --> 19:00.931
-Showing off.
-Right, I see.

19:02.474 --> 19:05.811
Still, I'm glad
I'm someone you'd want to show off.

19:08.313 --> 19:09.148
Thanks.

19:12.985 --> 19:15.154
So what did you want to tell me?

19:22.035 --> 19:23.078
Ms. Shin Ji-sun.

19:24.955 --> 19:25.873
Will you

19:27.040 --> 19:27.958
marry me?

19:33.463 --> 19:34.298
What?

19:43.348 --> 19:44.516
Let's get married.

19:58.030 --> 19:59.281
What are you waiting for?

20:00.407 --> 20:02.743
Ji-sun, what are you waiting for? Say yes!

20:02.826 --> 20:03.827
Go on, say yes!

20:03.911 --> 20:05.579
-Guys, cut it out!
-Say yes!

20:05.662 --> 20:10.375
-Say yes!
-Say yes!

20:10.459 --> 20:12.878
-Say yes!
-Please!

20:15.505 --> 20:17.174
Say yes!

20:19.760 --> 20:23.222
I know it was out of nowhere,
but I couldn't think of any other option.

20:24.139 --> 20:26.350
Because I never want us to break up.

20:27.601 --> 20:29.102
Who said we're breaking up?

20:30.771 --> 20:33.398
I'm going to the UK
to work for a sports agency.

20:34.566 --> 20:35.817
I even met my new client.

20:38.028 --> 20:40.781
It's always been my dream,
so I can't give it up,

20:42.032 --> 20:43.575
but I can't leave without you.

20:44.368 --> 20:46.954
What, you think I'll cheat on you
if you're not around?

20:47.871 --> 20:49.164
Would you really?

20:51.917 --> 20:54.253
I won't ask you to come with me,
so just marry me.

20:54.878 --> 20:55.837
I won't.

20:56.964 --> 20:59.591
Getting married won't be necessary.

21:03.762 --> 21:05.138
Instead, let's go together.

21:07.224 --> 21:10.644
After the show, I was planning
to take a year off to study.

21:11.937 --> 21:14.398
I'd planned it
while preparing for the wedding,

21:14.481 --> 21:18.110
and even after calling off the engagement,
I was going to stick to the plan.

21:19.444 --> 21:23.448
I had planned to study in the US,
but I can just go to a different country.

21:24.449 --> 21:25.993
And you hadn't told me?

21:29.162 --> 21:30.956
I'd been hesitating because of you.

21:33.166 --> 21:35.127
I thought maybe
I should give up on my plan,

21:35.711 --> 21:38.714
but then wondered
if I was getting ahead of myself…

21:41.550 --> 21:43.802
Thank you for hesitating for my sake.

21:54.271 --> 21:57.899
I caught your strong dialect earlier.
I was impressed.

21:58.859 --> 22:00.193
I speak two languages.

22:00.277 --> 22:02.696
My mom's Busan dialect
and Dad's Seoul dialect.

22:03.739 --> 22:04.740
What about English?

22:05.240 --> 22:07.117
You seemed pretty fluent last time.

22:07.701 --> 22:08.952
Gee…

22:09.995 --> 22:10.829
H…

22:35.562 --> 22:39.107
I sleep well these days even without meds,
and I don't see Do Ra-mi.

22:39.649 --> 22:43.653
But I wonder
why I don't see Do Ra-mi anymore.

22:45.113 --> 22:46.865
I've given it some thought,

22:47.908 --> 22:52.621
and I shared a lifelong secret
with someone I deeply rely on.

22:53.413 --> 22:54.790
I think that might be why.

22:55.499 --> 22:56.875
What kind of secret was it?

22:57.709 --> 22:59.211
It's about my childhood.

23:00.170 --> 23:04.091
Then perhaps Do Ra-mi is related
to your childhood, Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

23:06.176 --> 23:08.595
Do Ra-mi couldn't have existed
when I was a kid.

23:08.678 --> 23:11.515
Perhaps you only thought it was Do Ra-mi

23:11.598 --> 23:14.059
because your symptoms began
after filming that movie.

23:15.102 --> 23:16.937
Was the person you were seeing

23:17.437 --> 23:19.356
really Do Ra-mi?

23:25.987 --> 23:30.158
I was sure it was Do Ra-mi,
but he said it might not be her.

23:30.659 --> 23:33.370
Didn't she tell you herself
that she was Do Ra-mi?

23:33.870 --> 23:36.623
She said everything came
from your own head.

23:37.332 --> 23:39.709
Maybe she said that
because it's what you believed.

23:40.210 --> 23:42.170
She looked like me, was terrifying,

23:42.254 --> 23:45.298
and kept criticizing me.
Naturally, I thought she was Do Ra-mi.

23:46.258 --> 23:47.968
Are you still at the hospital?

23:48.051 --> 23:51.346
No, I'm shopping for Yong-u's present.

23:52.556 --> 23:54.766
I feel like I'm sending away
my baby brother.

23:55.684 --> 23:57.519
-Are you at home, Ho-jin?
-Yes.

23:58.103 --> 23:59.771
I'm waiting for a guest.

23:59.855 --> 24:00.689
A guest?

24:01.565 --> 24:02.899
The novelist?

24:03.692 --> 24:04.568
No.

24:05.068 --> 24:06.611
I'll tell you about it next time.

24:07.195 --> 24:10.157
What do you mean "next time"?
See you this evening.

24:21.293 --> 24:25.547
Perhaps you didn't emerge
due to a rapid change in her environment

24:25.630 --> 24:27.507
but from a much deeper

24:29.176 --> 24:31.428
and darker past.

24:43.690 --> 24:45.484
Do you have this in a larger size?

24:45.567 --> 24:47.652
-Sure, let me check for you.
-Thank you.

24:54.784 --> 24:56.119
Picking out a present?

25:09.549 --> 25:13.595
I heard that Mr. Yoon
had quite a formidable collection,

25:14.095 --> 25:15.430
but seeing it in person,

25:16.056 --> 25:18.183
it's even more impressive than I imagined.

25:18.975 --> 25:22.312
I heard you had something
you insisted on telling me in person.

25:22.896 --> 25:23.772
Right.

25:24.272 --> 25:28.902
First, I wanted to ask you
to consider donating to our foundation.

25:28.985 --> 25:31.655
Everything here is my mother's.
It's not mine to give away.

25:34.574 --> 25:38.286
It seems Mu-hee has given you
an unfavorable impression of us.

25:39.454 --> 25:42.874
I wonder just how terribly you treated her
to assume that right away.

25:44.751 --> 25:46.711
We were fairly strict with her.

25:47.587 --> 25:51.424
She's a cunning girl, apt at telling lies
depending on the circumstances.

25:51.508 --> 25:54.261
Sounds like she was a clever person
who caught on fast

25:55.387 --> 25:59.224
to the fact that she could never be honest
in a place shrouded by lies.

26:07.357 --> 26:09.985
You pretended to be selfless as a child,

26:10.068 --> 26:13.655
but now that you're somewhat famous,
you seem to want things out of your reach.

26:16.157 --> 26:18.243
I'm not just somewhat famous.

26:18.743 --> 26:20.579
I've earned so much money

26:21.496 --> 26:23.582
that these things
are well within my reach.

26:24.958 --> 26:26.626
Now you're the very image of her.

26:28.461 --> 26:29.337
What do you mean?

26:31.381 --> 26:34.718
Your uncle has gone to meet
the maternal grandson of Mr. Yoon Won-jae.

26:37.095 --> 26:39.139
We had no choice
but to tell him about you.

26:39.931 --> 26:42.309
His family could be of great help to us.

26:43.727 --> 26:45.729
Don't try to own things
that don't suit you

26:46.396 --> 26:49.065
simply because things are starting
to look up for you.

26:54.154 --> 26:55.196
Aunt.

27:03.538 --> 27:05.957
The woman who gave birth to Mu-hee
was not family.

27:09.085 --> 27:11.921
My brother never married that woman.

27:12.422 --> 27:15.592
She tried to use that child
to stop him from leaving her.

27:16.384 --> 27:18.803
And when that didn't work out
like she'd hoped,

27:18.887 --> 27:21.514
she caused a huge tragedy
in an attempt to ruin everything.

27:23.808 --> 27:25.518
That's the kind of mother she had.

27:26.978 --> 27:28.563
It's a shameful part of our history

27:29.147 --> 27:30.732
that we wanted to keep hidden.

27:33.652 --> 27:36.071
I heard you were quite close to her.

27:36.780 --> 27:40.200
I requested to meet
because I had to share this with you.

27:40.283 --> 27:43.119
If that were the case,
you shouldn't have come all this way.

27:44.245 --> 27:45.997
Mu-hee already told me everything.

27:49.793 --> 27:51.628
She told you about herself?

27:51.711 --> 27:55.006
He already knows. I told him everything.

27:57.717 --> 27:58.593
You told him?

27:58.677 --> 28:01.346
I told him. Everything.

28:03.014 --> 28:04.057
Everything?

28:12.899 --> 28:13.983
I knew it.

28:15.151 --> 28:19.322
So you do remember
what happened to your parents that day.

28:25.620 --> 28:28.039
I was simply terrified.

28:29.499 --> 28:33.336
I told you I didn't remember
because I was scared you'd kick me out.

28:35.839 --> 28:37.507
I remember everything.

28:41.720 --> 28:45.390
Happy birthday, Mu-hee.

29:29.559 --> 29:30.518
Mu-hee.

29:30.602 --> 29:32.187
You should eat some too.

29:34.063 --> 29:36.065
Let's all be happy together.

29:38.109 --> 29:40.737
That woman laced
her daughter's birthday cake with poison

29:41.404 --> 29:43.072
and tried to die with her.

29:44.908 --> 29:47.243
Perhaps the girl refused and tried to run

29:47.786 --> 29:49.454
because she fell off the balcony.

29:51.414 --> 29:53.792
She said she had no memories
of that horrid incident,

29:55.251 --> 29:57.045
which we thought was a relief.

29:58.671 --> 30:00.131
You turned your back on her.

30:01.758 --> 30:03.009
Ever since she was a child,

30:03.760 --> 30:06.513
Ms. Cha Mu-hee has carried
the weight of those awful memories

30:07.722 --> 30:09.224
entirely on her own.

30:10.183 --> 30:12.227
I pitied her, yes,
but she was her daughter.

30:12.310 --> 30:13.853
She made our skin crawl.

30:19.901 --> 30:22.362
There's only one photo I didn't destroy.

30:25.990 --> 30:29.118
I intended to show it to Mu-hee
if she ever brought up her mom.

30:29.702 --> 30:32.163
See for yourself
why we find that girl so terrifying.

30:34.833 --> 30:35.792
It wasn't my fault.

30:37.168 --> 30:38.545
So why did you

30:39.337 --> 30:40.421
hate me so much?

30:43.800 --> 30:45.009
We were afraid.

30:46.386 --> 30:47.720
We were so afraid of you.

30:50.265 --> 30:51.391
If you remember,

30:52.433 --> 30:55.228
you must also remember your mom.

30:59.274 --> 31:00.275
Then again,

31:01.276 --> 31:02.735
there's no way you couldn't.

31:03.903 --> 31:07.198
Seeing that face in the mirror every day,

31:08.783 --> 31:11.536
you couldn't possibly forget your mom.

31:37.854 --> 31:39.105
Mom.

31:43.526 --> 31:47.488
She looked like me, was terrifying,
and kept criticizing me.

31:47.989 --> 31:49.866
Naturally, I thought she was Do Ra-mi.

31:58.791 --> 32:02.128
If that face wasn't Do Ra-mi's,
then whose could it be?

32:15.475 --> 32:16.684
It was my mom.

32:18.478 --> 32:19.479
Do Ra-mi

32:20.688 --> 32:22.440
had my mom's face.

32:25.902 --> 32:27.695
At last, you recognize me.

32:31.032 --> 32:31.866
Here.

32:32.450 --> 32:34.202
Let's all be happy now.

32:35.036 --> 32:36.245
You should eat some too.

32:41.417 --> 32:42.627
I don't want to.

32:43.419 --> 32:46.673
The chicks died after eating the cake.

32:47.340 --> 32:48.716
And Dad too.

32:48.800 --> 32:50.677
You want to be left behind all alone?

32:54.722 --> 32:55.556
Why?

32:56.265 --> 32:57.600
There would be no one

32:58.267 --> 33:00.561
left in this world to love you.

33:01.896 --> 33:03.982
You could never be happy.

33:04.524 --> 33:05.692
I still don't want it.

33:29.132 --> 33:30.008
Mom.

33:49.652 --> 33:51.070
That day,

33:51.779 --> 33:54.574
I never fully managed
to get away from my mom.

33:55.616 --> 33:58.453
Her words that I'd never be happy

33:59.078 --> 34:01.998
kept coming back to me,
no matter how hard I tried to erase them,

34:02.498 --> 34:05.293
and haunted me my entire life.

34:11.883 --> 34:14.427
So this time, I must use all I have

34:14.927 --> 34:16.804
to try once more

34:18.181 --> 34:20.600
to truly break free from this delusion.

34:21.601 --> 34:23.603
Please try your darndest

34:24.145 --> 34:25.855
so I can finally get lost.

34:27.607 --> 34:28.733
Goodbye.

34:39.660 --> 34:40.870
Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

34:42.038 --> 34:43.081
I love you.

34:54.801 --> 34:57.386
Ms. Cha Mu-hee, are you with us?

35:19.659 --> 35:22.537
You were out for three days.
I was so worried, Mu-hee.

35:24.122 --> 35:26.457
I thought you'd be out for a while,
like last time.

35:28.709 --> 35:30.670
Hey, I'm fine.

35:30.753 --> 35:32.672
Even the doctor said I'm fine.

35:34.590 --> 35:36.592
I contacted Mr. Joo.

35:36.676 --> 35:38.928
He's on his way,
so he should be here soon.

35:39.011 --> 35:39.846
He will?

35:41.973 --> 35:45.518
Hey, give me a mirror.
I haven't washed my hair.

35:45.601 --> 35:46.602
I guess you're back.

35:47.186 --> 35:48.396
Thank goodness.

35:48.479 --> 35:50.398
It would've killed Mr. Joo otherwise.

35:52.108 --> 35:53.568
He couldn't stay here,

35:53.651 --> 35:56.362
what with all the reporters
and the show's crew visiting.

35:56.445 --> 35:58.781
He was withering away at home,
unable to sleep.

36:51.667 --> 36:52.668
Hiro!

36:53.711 --> 36:55.963
Ms. Cha Mu-hee is awake.

36:56.047 --> 36:57.215
Really? Is she okay?

36:57.298 --> 37:00.885
I spoke to Mr. Kim Yong-u on the phone,
and he said she's well.

37:03.596 --> 37:05.056
I knew it.

37:05.598 --> 37:08.768
There's no way
a zombie would die so easily.

37:10.144 --> 37:11.437
Oh no. I'm exhausted.

37:11.520 --> 37:13.898
Hey, are you okay?

37:15.691 --> 37:18.527
You've spent three days
going at it with that punching bag.

37:19.195 --> 37:21.739
I was worried you might collapse too.

37:22.240 --> 37:24.116
I won't collapse from this!

37:27.745 --> 37:30.623
Take this off.
I don't have the strength to do it myself.

37:38.047 --> 37:40.675
Your hands are trembling.

37:40.758 --> 37:43.678
-I'm fine.
-You shouldn't overexert yourself.

37:47.056 --> 37:48.683
This is all that zombie's fault.

37:49.684 --> 37:52.186
When I see her,
I'm going to get my revenge.

37:52.770 --> 37:54.897
Why are you always going on about revenge?

38:13.749 --> 38:16.127
We really do look alike.

38:16.210 --> 38:20.172
She's not the same person as you,
Ms. Cha Mu-hee. Not at all.

38:23.884 --> 38:25.469
I know.

38:30.266 --> 38:31.142
Mu-hee.

38:33.144 --> 38:35.479
There's something you still don't know.

38:50.077 --> 38:50.995
That day,

38:52.788 --> 38:54.248
on your birthday,

38:55.541 --> 38:57.460
someone reported that a child had fallen,

38:58.210 --> 39:00.087
so the police entered your home.

39:01.255 --> 39:04.258
Thanks to that,
your parents were found and saved.

39:07.762 --> 39:08.721
Then…

39:12.350 --> 39:13.434
They're still alive.

39:17.646 --> 39:21.400
The father you thought had passed away
was actually your youngest uncle.

39:22.151 --> 39:23.486
So your father

39:24.111 --> 39:26.530
is actually your uncle who lives abroad.

39:31.243 --> 39:32.578
I had no idea.

39:34.080 --> 39:37.833
Even as a kid,
I didn't get to see my dad very often,

39:39.418 --> 39:41.545
so I had no idea what he looked like.

39:42.046 --> 39:45.633
Apparently, no one knows the whereabouts
of your mother since the incident,

39:46.550 --> 39:48.177
but she's definitely alive.

39:52.223 --> 39:53.891
Then why did they tell me…

39:56.018 --> 39:57.978
that both of them died that day?

40:02.233 --> 40:04.568
You said you didn't remember the incident,

40:05.778 --> 40:07.905
so they covered up the events of that day.

40:09.990 --> 40:11.867
Your father's family deceived you.

40:25.256 --> 40:26.715
So they were alive.

42:22.206 --> 42:26.043
I desperately wanted to join this project,
so I shot that in a hurry.

42:26.126 --> 42:27.962
Thank you for your kind words.

42:48.274 --> 42:51.569
I prepared some words to say on my own,
without an interpreter.

43:25.019 --> 43:26.687
You've changed, Hiro.

43:28.314 --> 43:29.440
You've matured.

43:55.633 --> 43:58.427
Your father said
he couldn't bear to see you,

43:59.428 --> 44:01.639
so we had no choice but to take you in.

44:02.348 --> 44:05.392
I'm not here to blame you.

44:08.854 --> 44:10.272
I came to ask you for a favor.

44:13.067 --> 44:16.070
The only one who can find out
where my mom is now

44:16.153 --> 44:17.321
is, in the end,

44:18.030 --> 44:20.199
my father, who was closest to her.

44:23.911 --> 44:25.162
Please ask that man…

44:27.289 --> 44:29.083
to at least find that out for me.

44:31.001 --> 44:32.961
You're going to meet your mom?

44:35.422 --> 44:37.549
I need to see that she's alive
with my own two eyes.

44:38.050 --> 44:40.344
I think it's the only way
to be truly free of her.

44:42.680 --> 44:43.681
All right.

44:49.061 --> 44:52.606
I have to say I'm a little worried.

44:54.441 --> 44:56.068
Don't you worry.

44:56.151 --> 44:57.569
There's always Papago.

44:58.070 --> 45:00.989
And it's Koreatown,
so I won't even need to use Papago.

45:01.615 --> 45:03.992
I could go with you, you know.

45:04.493 --> 45:07.663
Not as an interpreter,
but just as moral support.

45:11.875 --> 45:13.127
Mr. Joo Ho-jin.

45:14.169 --> 45:15.879
I told myself

45:16.547 --> 45:18.632
that we'll never have a happy ending.

45:20.551 --> 45:23.679
So you, not wanting me to be anxious,

45:25.055 --> 45:28.851
said all that nonsense about how it's fine
'cause we'll definitely break up.

45:32.938 --> 45:35.858
I don't want us to definitely break up.

45:37.526 --> 45:38.944
So let's…

45:42.698 --> 45:45.075
break up right here this time.

45:51.415 --> 45:55.210
I'll come back and threaten you
into dating me again.

45:56.545 --> 45:57.379
When I do,

45:58.505 --> 46:01.675
please give in so we can be happy together
for a very long time.

46:10.642 --> 46:12.853
I'm not one to give in to threats.

46:12.936 --> 46:15.481
You'd better come prepared
and bring your worst.

46:16.732 --> 46:17.566
I will.

47:04.488 --> 47:06.073
I wonder how she's doing.

47:07.866 --> 47:10.577
Can I pack some of your gochujang
to bring to the UK?

47:10.661 --> 47:12.454
Your housekeeper makes it so well.

47:12.955 --> 47:14.081
Sure. Take some.

47:15.123 --> 47:15.958
Hey, Mr. Joo.

47:17.960 --> 47:19.795
Can I take some soy sauce too?

47:20.712 --> 47:21.630
Go on.

47:22.172 --> 47:23.423
Where was it again?

47:24.675 --> 47:25.968
Under the sink…

47:26.051 --> 47:27.719
-The sink?
-I'll find it for you.

47:27.803 --> 47:28.804
No, it's okay.

47:30.889 --> 47:33.183
Why did he bring that pot in from outside…

47:36.228 --> 47:37.312
-Found it?
-Found it.

47:38.230 --> 47:39.273
-A container…
-Take it.

47:39.773 --> 47:41.316
-Mr. Joo, I--
-Just take it all!

47:41.817 --> 47:42.651
All of it.

47:44.653 --> 47:47.447
Ji-sun's rubbing off on you
in all sorts of weird ways.

47:50.868 --> 47:52.995
Why did you bring this bag here?

47:59.084 --> 48:00.002
Give them to me.

48:00.878 --> 48:04.298
I'll be donating my father's books
to the university library,

48:04.798 --> 48:09.094
but let's think about what to do
with the other antiques and paintings.

48:09.845 --> 48:12.264
Can't you deal with them all
while you're here?

48:12.347 --> 48:16.685
Hey, those are all invaluable pieces.
I can't sort through them all in one go.

48:17.519 --> 48:19.855
I'll take my time with it
over several visits.

48:19.938 --> 48:21.940
And keep using this house
as a storage unit?

48:22.816 --> 48:23.692
Why?

48:24.568 --> 48:27.654
Do you want to sell this house
and buy an apartment for marriage?

48:30.908 --> 48:31.742
Hey.

48:33.744 --> 48:35.954
Can I have this book?

48:36.038 --> 48:37.331
-It's yours.
-Really?

48:39.124 --> 48:40.250
Then

48:41.043 --> 48:42.502
how about this one?

48:42.586 --> 48:43.545
As you wish.

48:44.046 --> 48:45.339
That's a first edition Dickens.

48:46.465 --> 48:47.799
Oh my, not the Dickens.

48:47.883 --> 48:49.593
-Just let me have it.
-I'll take that.

48:49.676 --> 48:51.094
Hey, no take-backs!

48:51.178 --> 48:54.848
-Why have you gotten so greedy?
-You wouldn't even take good care of them!

48:54.932 --> 48:55.974
I will.

48:56.058 --> 48:57.184
Hold up!

48:57.267 --> 49:01.063
First, you toy with someone's heart,
and now you're doing the same with a book.

49:07.361 --> 49:10.238
Sell this house and move…

49:13.533 --> 49:15.661
But Ms. Cha Mu-hee liked this house.

49:41.436 --> 49:44.231
This year, we're all celebrating
New Year's Eve together.

49:44.731 --> 49:45.941
You'll join us, won't you?

49:46.441 --> 49:48.527
-Sure.
-We'll be expecting you.

49:48.610 --> 49:51.196
So the whole gang is coming this time?

49:51.279 --> 49:53.865
Of course. Everyone will be there.

49:53.949 --> 49:57.452
Can't you bring your girlfriend with you?

49:58.537 --> 49:59.454
I can't.

50:00.288 --> 50:01.540
We're broken up right now.

50:02.040 --> 50:05.002
Come on. You got dumped again?

50:09.047 --> 50:09.965
I'm off.

50:10.716 --> 50:14.970
Hey, it's okay if you're late,
so join us instead of staying home alone.

50:15.053 --> 50:16.555
-Okay.
-Bye.

50:28.900 --> 50:31.778
You're the absolute best.

50:31.862 --> 50:32.904
Everyone!

50:32.988 --> 50:33.989
Today's the day

50:34.072 --> 50:38.118
we submitted the final cut
of Romantic Trip!

50:40.328 --> 50:45.417
We almost missed the deadline.
The penalty is a couple hundred million.

50:45.500 --> 50:49.254
My hands were trembling
as I was typing out the captions.

50:49.337 --> 50:50.881
You'd better toughen up a little.

50:50.964 --> 50:55.052
Once it airs and the ratings are in,
your whole body will be shaking.

50:55.135 --> 50:56.386
Oh, come on…

50:56.470 --> 50:58.680
I'm not worried. Our show's great.

50:58.764 --> 51:00.098
Of course you're not worried.

51:00.182 --> 51:03.727
You're running away to the UK
before the numbers come out.

51:04.227 --> 51:05.062
She's right.

51:05.645 --> 51:07.898
-Hey, what's that?
-What's that?

51:07.981 --> 51:10.734
Which is why I'm buying tonight.

51:12.277 --> 51:15.447
Despite the producer changing
partway through filming,

51:15.530 --> 51:17.449
you all did a great job.

51:17.532 --> 51:19.910
-Shall we raise a glass?
-Let's raise a glass!

51:19.993 --> 51:22.287
Hello, everyone!

51:22.788 --> 51:24.998
-Welcome.
-Hey, you're here!

51:25.082 --> 51:27.501
I heard you turned in the cut.
Good work, all.

51:27.584 --> 51:28.543
It was nothing.

51:28.627 --> 51:31.713
Our show is going to be a huge hit.
You know that, right?

51:33.965 --> 51:35.592
Our company card. Today's on me.

51:35.675 --> 51:37.177
-Okay!
-Wow!

51:37.260 --> 51:40.305
Hey, so you show up like this
out of nowhere?

51:40.388 --> 51:42.349
Man, I was so shocked.

51:42.432 --> 51:44.768
You're going to ride on our coattails?

51:44.851 --> 51:47.938
He'll start with the tails,
then just wear the coat.

51:48.021 --> 51:51.149
Didn't you see this coming?
This is how Producer Kim plays the game.

51:51.233 --> 51:52.859
-Right.
-Merry Christmas!

51:52.943 --> 51:55.862
-Merry Christmas!
-Merry Christmas!

51:55.946 --> 51:57.405
Thanks for dinner!

52:48.415 --> 52:49.416
Babe.

52:50.500 --> 52:52.169
Want to go see the stars with me?

52:53.086 --> 52:55.505
What a succinct but effective threat.

53:07.225 --> 53:10.437
Welcome, and thank you
for visiting our observatory.

53:10.937 --> 53:12.731
The International Dark Sky Association,

53:12.814 --> 53:16.735
dedicated to protecting the night sky
from artificial light,

53:16.818 --> 53:20.488
certified this site
as Asia's first dark-sky preserve.

53:20.572 --> 53:23.950
Here, you can observe celestial wonders
like the Milky Way

53:24.034 --> 53:26.536
and shooting stars with the naked eye.

53:27.329 --> 53:29.956
As the lights go out
and darkness settles in,

53:30.040 --> 53:33.668
the stars will begin to appear one by one.

53:34.252 --> 53:37.088
We hope you have
an unforgettable night here

53:37.172 --> 53:40.383
at our observatory with someone special.

53:49.809 --> 53:51.478
Have you come to see the stars?

54:06.034 --> 54:08.286
You need to do a good job
interpreting today.

54:08.787 --> 54:12.666
He might be really mad at me
because I took so long.

54:13.667 --> 54:15.543
Please translate with all your heart.

54:19.714 --> 54:21.174
I've missed you.

54:27.389 --> 54:29.140
I guess English doesn't work on him.

54:30.934 --> 54:32.269
Let's try Japanese.

54:36.648 --> 54:38.316
I really missed you.

54:45.031 --> 54:46.866
Does he still not understand me?

54:56.376 --> 54:58.503
I missed you so much.

54:59.838 --> 55:01.506
So much that it almost killed me.

55:15.687 --> 55:18.648
Why aren't you reacting?
You understood everything.

55:21.192 --> 55:23.153
Why aren't you saying anything back?

55:25.947 --> 55:27.240
Are you really mad at me?

55:32.412 --> 55:35.915
I was having trouble
finding the right words to reply with.

55:39.252 --> 55:40.920
"Have you come to see the stars?"

55:47.302 --> 55:49.304
I even brought a bouquet of clovers…

55:51.598 --> 55:53.892
so that we'd have clear skies.

56:01.858 --> 56:04.402
If you're mad at me, you can swear at me.

56:06.279 --> 56:07.655
If you'd rather not talk,

56:09.157 --> 56:11.659
you can use a universal language.

56:14.329 --> 56:15.205
Sure.

56:16.414 --> 56:17.415
That option

56:18.875 --> 56:20.085
seems most appropriate.

57:42.667 --> 57:44.335
Finally,

57:45.503 --> 57:47.297
we've reached our happy ending.

57:49.299 --> 57:50.133
Wait.

57:51.301 --> 57:52.635
Let's change the music.

57:53.845 --> 57:57.015
Because our ending
will be a perfectly happy one.

58:11.821 --> 58:14.782
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

01:00:35.048 --> 01:00:40.053
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
